[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3988856674","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116964#issuecomment-3988856674","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116964","id":3988856674,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7twR9i","user":{"login":"bruvzg","id":7645683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDU2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7645683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg","html_url":"https://github.com/bruvzg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-03T06:03:25Z","updated_at":"2026-03-03T06:03:25Z","body":"I was not able to reproduce it on Windows 11 or macOS 26 (with current master and 4.6.1), disk activity goes to zero right after loading is done, and is not going over 30% usage while loading.\n\n> load any project.\n\nIs it reproducible with new, empty project?\n\n> it does NOT happen with the project load screen when your first boot the Editor, you have to actually load a project first\n\nProject manager is always running with Compatibility (OpenGL) renderer, are affected projects using Mobile/Forward+ renderer? Disk activity might be related to shader cache.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3988856674/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3989157628","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116964#issuecomment-3989157628","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116964","id":3989157628,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7txbb8","user":{"login":"Pixelmusement","id":78319361,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc4MzE5MzYx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/78319361?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pixelmusement","html_url":"https://github.com/Pixelmusement","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pixelmusement/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pixelmusement/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pixelmusement/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pixelmusement/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pixelmusement/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pixelmusement/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pixelmusement/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pixelmusement/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pixelmusement/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-03T07:12:53Z","updated_at":"2026-03-03T07:18:52Z","body":"> Is it reproducible with new, empty project?\n\nNo... in fact, working with a brand new project this problem is not manifesting at all despite adding various nodes and shaders...\n\nInteresting... I'm doing some more checking and I've noticed something curious: This problem is ONLY manifesting with projects which I have migrated from an earlier version of Godot Engine to 4.6. I tried migrating a project just now which has literally nothing more in it than a 2D scene, a sprite, and 6 lines of code, and the problem manifested. If I recreate the entire thing from scratch, the problem does not manifest.\n\nHere's a zip of the project prior to migration. If I migrate and load the project into 4.6, the disk usage problem manifests, and furthermore, will now happen any time the project is loaded or run. (EDIT: Even if I delete the shader cache manually prior to loading in the Godot Editor.)\n\n[wctrltest_notmigrated.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/25708241/wctrltest_notmigrated.zip)","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3989157628/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3991524460","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116964#issuecomment-3991524460","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116964","id":3991524460,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7t6dRs","user":{"login":"bruvzg","id":7645683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDU2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7645683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg","html_url":"https://github.com/bruvzg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-03T14:40:53Z","updated_at":"2026-03-03T14:40:53Z","body":"I can't reproduce it with this project or converted projects either.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3991524460/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3991611574","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116964#issuecomment-3991611574","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116964","id":3991611574,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7t6yi2","user":{"login":"Pixelmusement","id":78319361,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc4MzE5MzYx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/78319361?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pixelmusement","html_url":"https://github.com/Pixelmusement","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pixelmusement/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pixelmusement/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pixelmusement/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pixelmusement/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pixelmusement/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pixelmusement/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pixelmusement/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pixelmusement/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pixelmusement/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-03T14:54:51Z","updated_at":"2026-03-03T15:03:02Z","body":"I suppose at this point I should at least prove I'm not crazy:\n\n()EDIT: System access being as high as it is was in the screenshot is a coincidence. Normally it's just as low as everything else while this is going on; I just happened to screencap exactly when something unrelated fired off in the background.)\n\n<img width=\"1920\" height=\"1032\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/5522c01f-a853-4968-bff4-eaf00cc52008\" />\n<img width=\"1920\" height=\"1032\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/4ea08428-b823-4adc-98f3-2901bbaeac7d\" />","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3991611574/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3993135286","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116964#issuecomment-3993135286","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116964","id":3993135286,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7uAmi2","user":{"login":"Screenhog","id":1479412,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0Nzk0MTI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1479412?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Screenhog","html_url":"https://github.com/Screenhog","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Screenhog/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Screenhog/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Screenhog/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Screenhog/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Screenhog/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Screenhog/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Screenhog/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Screenhog/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Screenhog/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-03T19:42:18Z","updated_at":"2026-03-03T19:42:18Z","body":"I'm having a similar issue, though it might not be the same. For me, once I launch Godot, it'll go to the project menu screen, but after that my CPU jumps to 100% and just stays there. It shows \"System Interrupts\" at 100% CPU usage.\n\nIt's tough to pin down whether or not Godot is the cause, but I haven't observed this from any other application.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3993135286/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3993328669","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116964#issuecomment-3993328669","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116964","id":3993328669,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7uBVwd","user":{"login":"Pixelmusement","id":78319361,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc4MzE5MzYx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/78319361?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pixelmusement","html_url":"https://github.com/Pixelmusement","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pixelmusement/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pixelmusement/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pixelmusement/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pixelmusement/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pixelmusement/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pixelmusement/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pixelmusement/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pixelmusement/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pixelmusement/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-03T20:22:21Z","updated_at":"2026-03-03T20:22:21Z","body":"> I'm having a similar issue, though it might not be the same. For me, once I launch Godot, it'll go to the project menu screen, but after that my CPU jumps to 100% and just stays there. It shows \"System Interrupts\" at 100% CPU usage.\n> \n> It's tough to pin down whether or not Godot is the cause, but I haven't observed this from any other application.\n\n100% CPU usage on \"System Interrupts\" is almost always caused by a hardware failure or a driver problem. I would suggest reinstalling your graphics drivers as that would be my first assumption given that Godot Engine is what's causing this.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3993328669/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3995500757","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116964#issuecomment-3995500757","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116964","id":3995500757,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7uJoDV","user":{"login":"Screenhog","id":1479412,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0Nzk0MTI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1479412?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Screenhog","html_url":"https://github.com/Screenhog","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Screenhog/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Screenhog/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Screenhog/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Screenhog/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Screenhog/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Screenhog/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Screenhog/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Screenhog/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Screenhog/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-04T05:59:38Z","updated_at":"2026-03-04T05:59:38Z","body":"> > I'm having a similar issue, though it might not be the same. For me, once I launch Godot, it'll go to the project menu screen, but after that my CPU jumps to 100% and just stays there. It shows \"System Interrupts\" at 100% CPU usage.\n> > It's tough to pin down whether or not Godot is the cause, but I haven't observed this from any other application.\n> \n> 100% CPU usage on \"System Interrupts\" is almost always caused by a hardware failure or a driver problem. I would suggest reinstalling your graphics drivers as that would be my first assumption given that Godot Engine is what's causing this.\n\nThat solved it. Uninstalled and reinstalled an NVidia driver. Thank you!","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3995500757/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4147894691","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116964#issuecomment-4147894691","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116964","id":4147894691,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc73O9mj","user":{"login":"Pixelmusement","id":78319361,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc4MzE5MzYx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/78319361?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pixelmusement","html_url":"https://github.com/Pixelmusement","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pixelmusement/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pixelmusement/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pixelmusement/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pixelmusement/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pixelmusement/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pixelmusement/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pixelmusement/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pixelmusement/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pixelmusement/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-28T11:28:21Z","updated_at":"2026-03-28T11:28:21Z","body":"Update: I think this issue might be specifically related to the Steam-released builds of the Godot Engine, which is what I have been using. I need to do more testing to see if that's the case but could someone else attempt to recreate this problem with a Steam build and see if that does the trick?","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4147894691/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4147903951","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116964#issuecomment-4147903951","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116964","id":4147903951,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc73O_3P","user":{"login":"bruvzg","id":7645683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDU2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7645683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg","html_url":"https://github.com/bruvzg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-28T11:35:12Z","updated_at":"2026-03-28T11:35:12Z","body":"The only differences in the Steam build are:\n- it is loading `steam_api64.dll` and calling `SteamAPI_InitFlat` to enable time tracking.\n- it's running in self-contained mode, so all settings and cache are stored in the same folder as executable instead of `AppData`.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4147903951/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4149444121","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116964#issuecomment-4149444121","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116964","id":4149444121,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc73U34Z","user":{"login":"Pixelmusement","id":78319361,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc4MzE5MzYx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/78319361?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pixelmusement","html_url":"https://github.com/Pixelmusement","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pixelmusement/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pixelmusement/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pixelmusement/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pixelmusement/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pixelmusement/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pixelmusement/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pixelmusement/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pixelmusement/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pixelmusement/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-29T05:03:27Z","updated_at":"2026-03-29T05:03:27Z","body":"Well, that's enough. I've downloaded the latest stable build of Godot outside of Steam, tested, and ran into no issues. I then loaded up the Steam build, loaded the same projects, extreme disk access came back. Went back to the non-Steam build, loaded up the same projects, extreme disk access was gone again.\n\nSOMETHING is going on with the Steam build.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4149444121/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":2},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4150297692","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116964#issuecomment-4150297692","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116964","id":4150297692,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc73YIRc","user":{"login":"Zireael07","id":4525388,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1MjUzODg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4525388?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zireael07","html_url":"https://github.com/Zireael07","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zireael07/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zireael07/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zireael07/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zireael07/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zireael07